Socket activation confusion. systemctl status ssh showed inactive (dead) and disabled, which looked like SSH was off. But ssh.socket was active (listening) on 0.0.0.0:22. Modern Ubuntu uses socket activation: systemd listens on port 22 and starts sshd on demand. Lesson: don't panic at an "inactive" service, check what triggers it.
The NAT wall (about to hit this). VM listens on port 22, but the host can't reach it because NAT is one-way. Fix: VirtualBox port forwarding, host port 2222 → guest port 22.
